---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /
---
{% from "frame.njk" import frame %}
{#- Start page. The letter and the pictures come from the old nibbida.com start page, with the text rewritten in a more formal publisher voice. -#}
<section class="hero start-hero">
<h1>There is a crack in everything,<br>that's how the light gets in.</h1>
<p class="intro">– Leonard Cohen</p>
</section>
<section class="letter" id="welcome">
<div class="letter-text">
<h2>The way in is the way out…</h2>
<p>The Internet can feel like a maze, built to hold our attention and make us forget where we were going. <em>Nibbidā</em> is meant to do the opposite. The word means disenchantment, a quiet turning away from what does not lead to freedom. Here nothing is sold, and nothing is asking for your attention.</p>
<h2>…and the way out is through.</h2>
<p>Nibbidā is a small, independent Dhamma publisher. It prepares books and resources for people who want to understand their own minds more deeply, and who, like the Buddha, take it that there <em>is</em> a way out of the labyrinth for those who walk through it with growing clarity and wisdom. Meditation is the core of that work. Around it there is much that helps: the texts, the languages, the places to practice.</p>
<p>I hope the work here is useful, and that some of you will want to take part in it. May it make your own study and practice a little easier.</p>
<p class="sign"><em>Jayadhamma Bhikkhu</em></p>
</div>
<figure class="letter-fig">{{ frame('/assets/images/start-cat.jpg', 'A long-haired cat with closed eyes, rainbow light falling across its face and body', 1208, 1133) }}</figure>
</section>
<section class="projects" id="projects">
<h2>Publications and projects</h2>
<p class="sub-intro">Books, archives and tools, offered freely.</p>
<div class="proj-grid">
{% for p in projects.projects %}
<article class="proj">
{% if p.ready %}<a class="proj-img" href="{{ p.url | url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">{% endif %}{{ frame(('/assets/images/' ~ p.image), p.alt, 1200, 675, 'wide') }}{% if p.ready %}</a>{% endif %}
<p class="tag">{{ p.tagline }}</p>
<h3>{{ p.title }}</h3>
<p>{{ p.text | mdInline | safe }}</p>
{% if p.ready %}<a class="quiet-link" href="{{ p.url | url }}">{{ p.link or "Open" }} ↗</a>{% else %}<span class="soon">coming soon</span>{% endif %}
</article>
{% endfor %}
</div>
</section>
<section class="hero pub">
<p class="kicker">Independent Dhamma publishing</p>
<h1>Books for<br>slow reading.</h1>
<div class="hero-bottom">
<p class="intro">Texts and teachings of the Buddhist path, prepared with care and offered freely.</p>
<div class="actions">
<a class="button" href="{{ '/resources/archive/' | url }}">Explore the archive</a>
<a class="quiet-link" href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">About Nibbidā ↗</a>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="feature" id="books">
<div class="cover">
<span class="imprint">NIBBIDĀ</span>
<span class="title">First<br>editions</span>
<img class="cover-maze" src="{{ '/assets/labyrinth-white.svg' | url }}" alt="">
<span class="author">IN PREPARATION</span>
</div>
<div class="feature-copy">
<p class="kicker">In preparation</p>
<h2>The first Nibbidā editions</h2>
<p>The first books are being prepared. Until they are ready, the Dhamma-Dāna Archive holds more than 300 freely given books to read or download.</p>
</div>
<div class="feature-actions">
<a class="button" href="{{ '/resources/archive/' | url }}">Open the archive</a>
</div>
</section>
<section class="library">
<div class="rail-title">
<h2>Ways into the reading</h2>
<a href="{{ '/resources/' | url }}">All resources ↗</a>
</div>
<div class="library-list">
<article>
<h3>Begin with the archive</h3>
<p>Over 300 books, given freely<br>as Dhamma-dāna.</p>
<a href="{{ '/resources/archive/' | url }}">Open the archive ↗</a>
</article>
<article>
<h3>Learn Pali</h3>
<p>Tools, courses and texts for the<br>language of the early texts.</p>
<a href="{{ '/resources/pali/' | url }}">Open the guide ↗</a>
</article>
<article>
<h3>Listen</h3>
<p>Talks and guided meditations<br>to stream or download.</p>
<a href="{{ '/audio/' | url }}">Open the audio page ↗</a>
</article>
</div>
</section>
{%- if passages.items and passages.items.length %}
<section class="reading" id="reading">
<div class="reading-head">
<p class="kicker">A passage to sit with</p>
<span class="passage-count" aria-live="polite"></span>
</div>
<div class="passage-list">
{%- for q in passages.items %}
<div class="passage{% if loop.first %} on{% endif %}">
<div class="quote">
<p class="verse{% if q.text | length > 160 %} long{% endif %}">{{ q.text | trim | replace("\n", "<br>") | safe }}</p>
{{ "C5-B" | ornament("orn-c5b corner") | safe }}
</div>
<p class="note">{{ q.ref }} · {{ q.topic }}</p>
{%- if q.credit %}<p class="note credit-note">{{ q.credit }}</p>{% endif %}
</div>
{%- endfor %}
</div>
<div class="passages">
<button type="button" class="passage-btn" data-dir="-1" hidden>← Previous</button>
<button type="button" class="passage-btn" data-dir="1" hidden>Next passage →</button>
</div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
<section class="book-detail" id="book-detail">
<p class="kicker">About the publisher</p>
<div class="detail-row">
<div>
<h2>Nibbidā</h2>
<p>Nibbidā is a Dhamma publishing project run by Jayadhamma Bhikkhu, a Theravāda monk in the Forest tradition. It works on its own, without advertising, and relies on the generosity of its readers.</p>
</div>
<div class="actions">
<a class="quiet-link" href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">About ↗</a>
<a class="quiet-link" href="{{ '/donate/' | url }}">Donate ↗</a>
</div>
</div>
</section>
